it\n\n/dev/mapper/rhel-var-log-audit /var/log/audit xfs defaults,nodev,nosuid,noexec 0 0\n\nIf results are returned and the \"nodev\" option is missing, or if /var/log/audit is mounted without the \"nodev\" option, this is a finding.", "documentable": "false", "mitigations": "", "potential_impacts": "", "third_party_tools": "", "mitigation_control": "", "responsibility": "", "security_override_guidance": "", "ia_controls": "DCBP-1", "check_content_ref": {}, "legacy_ids": [], "ccis": ["CCI-001764"], "group_tree": [{"id": "V-230517", "title": "RHEL-08-040129", "description": ""}], "createdAt": "2026-06-15T16:15:57.323Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-15T16:15:57.323Z", "STIGUuid": "18722c88-ffa2-4ce9-b0e3-35717361716c", "status": "open", "overrides": {}, "comments": "", "finding_details": "/var/log/audit does not have a separate mount."}, {"uuid": "7b7e7462-8780-4c63-87fb-4b5926c1cec6", "stig_uuid": "18722c88-ffa2-4ce9-b0e3-35717361716c", "target_key": null, "stig_ref": null, "group_id": "V-230518", "rule_id": "SV-230518r958804", "rule_id_src": "SV-230518r958804_rule", "weight": "10.0", "classification": "Classified", "severity": "medium", "rule_version": "RHEL-08-040130", "group_title": "RHEL 8 must mount /var/log/audit with the nosuid option.", "rule_title": "RHEL 8 must mount /var/log/audit with the nosuid option.", "fix_text": "Configure the system so that /var/log/audit is mounted with the \"nosuid\" option by adding /modifying the /etc/fstab with the following line:\n\n/dev/mapper/rhel-var-log-audit /var/log/audit xfs defaults,nodev,nosuid,noexec 0 0", "false_positives": "", "false_negatives": "", "discussion": "The organization must identify authorized software programs and permit execution of authorized software. The process used to identify software programs that are authorized to execute on organizational information systems is commonly referred to as whitelisting.\n\nThe \"noexec\" mount option causes the system to not execute binary files. This option must be used